MINIKUBE TROUBLESHOOTING GUIDE
=============================

OVERVIEW
--------
This guide covers common Minikube installation and startup issues encountered while building the AI SRE Copilot project.

ISSUE #1 - kubectl get nodes
Connection Refused

Error:
The connection to the server localhost:8080 was refused.

Cause:
- kubectl installed
- Kubernetes cluster not started

Fix:
minikube start --driver=docker

Verify:
kubectl cluster-info
kubectl get nodes

Expected:
NAME       STATUS
minikube   Ready


ISSUE #2 - Docker Driver Should Not Be Used With Root

Error:
DRV_AS_ROOT
The docker driver should not be used with root privileges.

Cause:
Running Minikube as root.

Fix Option 1:
Use normal Linux user.

Fix Option 2:
minikube start --driver=docker --force

Alternative:
minikube start --driver=none


ISSUE #3 - API Server Connection Refused

Error:
Get https://192.168.49.2:8443
connection refused

Cause:
Minikube cluster stopped.

Check:
minikube status

Fix:
minikube start --driver=docker --force

Verify:
kubectl cluster-info


ISSUE #4 - Driver Not Supported

Error:
DRV_UNSUPPORTED_OS
The driver '' is not supported on linux/amd64

Cause:
Corrupted Minikube profile.

Fix:
minikube delete --all --purge

Restart:
minikube start --driver=docker --force


ISSUE #5 - Node Not Ready

Check:
kubectl get nodes

Output:
NotReady

Fix:
minikube status
systemctl status docker

Restart:
minikube stop
minikube start --driver=docker --force


ISSUE #6 - ErrImagePull

Error:
ErrImagePull
ImagePullBackOff

Cause:
Kubernetes cannot find Docker image.

Check:
docker images

Expected:
sre-copilot   latest

Load image:
minikube image load sre-copilot:latest

Restart deployment:
kubectl rollout restart deployment sre-copilot


ISSUE #7 - ImagePullBackOff

Error:
ImagePullBackOff

Cause:
Image missing inside Minikube.

Fix:
minikube image load sre-copilot:latest

Verify:
minikube image ls | grep sre-copilot


ISSUE #8 - Failed To Pull Image

Error:
pull access denied
repository does not exist

Cause:
Kubernetes trying to pull image from Docker Hub.

Fix:
Build image locally:

docker build -t sre-copilot:latest .

Load image:
minikube image load sre-copilot:latest


ISSUE #9 - Minikube Not Starting

Check Docker:
docker ps

Check Service:
systemctl status docker

Start Docker:
systemctl start docker

Retry:
minikube start --driver=docker


ISSUE #10 - Verify Complete Cluster

Commands:
minikube status
kubectl cluster-info
kubectl get nodes
kubectl get pods -A

Expected:
host: Running
kubelet: Running
apiserver: Running

Node:
minikube Ready


DEPLOYMENT CHECKLIST
--------------------
1. Docker Installed
2. Docker Running
3. kubectl Installed
4. Minikube Installed
5. Minikube Started
6. kubectl get nodes = Ready
7. Docker Image Built
8. Image Loaded Into Minikube
9. deployment.yaml Applied
10. service.yaml Applied


IMPORTANT COMMANDS
------------------

# start minikube
minikube start --driver=docker

# cluster information
kubectl cluster-info

# check nodes
kubectl get nodes

# check pods
kubectl get pods -A

# check services
kubectl get svc

# load image into minikube
minikube image load sre-copilot:latest

# restart deployment
kubectl rollout restart deployment sre-copilot

# monitor pods
kubectl get pods -w

